messages:   10%|#         | 61/600 [00:26<10:13,  1.14s/it][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nResearch suggests that compounds in meat may trigger wheezing in some children, which can lead to asthma or other respiratory problems. These compounds, known as advanced glycation end products, are released when meat is grilled at high temperatures. So eating a vegetarian diet or eating less meat can protect children from asthma risk.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings, if true, most questions the above statement?\n# Options:\nA) Meat roasting without high temperature does not produce advanced glycation end products, and its association with asthma is unknown\nB) Scientists have shown that advanced glycation end products in the body come mainly, but not exclusively, from meat\nC) Advanced glycation end products can not only cause asthma, but also accelerate human aging and cause various chronic degenerative diseases\nD) Advanced glycation end products, as proteins, occur naturally in the body and accumulate with age', "<think>.\nTo determine which option most questions the statement, we need to analyze each option and see how it relates to the context provided. The context states that advanced glycation end products (AGEs) are released when meat is grilled at high temperatures and can trigger wheezing in some children, leading to asthma or other respiratory problems. The statement suggests that eating a vegetarian diet or eating less meat can protect children from asthma risk.\n\nLet's evaluate each option:.\n\nA) Meat roasting without high temperature does not produce advanced glycation end products, and its association with asthma is unknown.\n- This option suggests that roasting meat at low temperatures does not produce AGEs, which would contradict the context. However, it does not directly question the statement's claim about the relationship between meat consumption and asthma risk.\n\nB) Scientists have shown that advanced glycation end products in the body come mainly, but not exclusively, from meat.\n- This option questions the specificity of the statement by suggesting that AGEs can come from sources other than meat. This would challenge the idea that eating less meat can protect children from asthma risk, as it implies that other dietary factors may also contribute to the development of asthma.\n\nC) Advanced glycation end products can not only cause asthma, but also accelerate human aging and cause various chronic degenerative diseases. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
