messages:   23%|##3       | 139/600 [03:31<03:11,  2.41it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nDing kiln is one of the five famous kilns in Song Dynasty, which is as famous as Ru, Guan, GE and Jun kilns. The kiln is located in Quyang, Hebei Province. Quyang County belonged to Dingzhou in the Song Dynasty, so it was named Ding kiln. Under the influence of Xing kiln, Ding kiln mainly produces white porcelain, but also burns black glaze and green glaze at the same time. The enamel of white porcelain is clear and moist, the color is mild, just like tooth carving, and the recessive is quite good. The decoration is well-known in ancient and modern times for its vivid and powerful carved and printed white porcelain, which is better than Xing kiln. The beautiful and elegant carved white porcelain and magnificent printed white porcelain in the Song and Jin dynasties are the two main varieties of Ding Kiln, representing the typical artistic style of Ding Kiln in its heyday.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings does not match the original text?\n# Options:\nA) The song dynasty and jin dynasty were the heyday of ding kiln.\nB) Engraved and printed white porcelain is the representative work of ding kiln.\nC) The white porcelain of ding kiln draws lessons from xing kiln and exceeds that of xing kiln.\nD) Beauty, simplicity and elegance are a typical artistic style of ding kiln.', "<think>.\nTo determine which option does not match the original text, let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) The Song dynasty and Jin dynasty were the heyday of Ding kiln.\n- The text mentions that Ding kiln was one of the five famous kilns in the Song Dynasty and Quyang County belonged to Dingzhou in the Song Dynasty. This suggests that the Song Dynasty was indeed the heyday of Ding kiln.\n\nB) Engraved and printed white porcelain is the representative work of Ding kiln.\n- The text states that the beautiful and elegant carved white porcelain and magnificent printed white porcelain in the Song and Jin dynasties are the two main varieties of Ding Kiln, representing the typical artistic style of Ding Kiln in its heyday. This indicates that engraved and printed white porcelain is indeed a representative work of Ding kiln.\n\nC) The white porcelain of Ding kiln draws lessons from Xing kiln and exceeds that of Xing kiln.\n- The text mentions that Ding kiln mainly produces white porcelain, which is clear and moist, the color is mild, just like tooth carving, and the recessive is quite good. It also states that the enamel of white porcelain is clear and moist, the color is mild, just like tooth carving, and the recessive is quite good. This suggests that Ding kiln's white porcelain draws lessons from Xing kiln and exceeds that of Xing kiln.\n\nD) Beauty, simplicity and elegance are a typical artistic style of Ding kiln.\n- The text mentions that the beautiful and elegant carved white porcelain and magnificent printed white porcelain in the Song and Jin dynasties are the two main varieties of Ding Kiln, representing the typical artistic style of Ding Kiln in its heyday. This suggests that beauty, simplicity, and elegance are indeed a typical artistic style of Ding kiln. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
