ty either pushed them into smaller orbits or drove them out of the solar system.\n\n2. **Identify the Given Information**:.\n   - We know that Jupiter's gravity either pushed them into smaller orbits or expelled them from the solar system.\n   - We also know that Jupiter's gravity either pushed them into smaller orbits or drove them out of the solar system.\n\n3. **Analyze the Options**:.\n   - Option A: Jupiter's gravity pushes them into smaller orbits and drives them out of the solar system.\n   - Option B: Jupiter's gravity did not push them into smaller orbits, but drove them out of the solar system.\n   - Option C: Jupiter's gravity pushed them into smaller orbits, but did not drive them out of the solar system.\n   - Option D: Jupiter's gravitational pull neither pushed them into smaller orbits nor drove them out of the solar system.\n\n4. **Determine the Valid Conclusion**:.\n   - Since only one of the two conclusions is true, we need to identify which option aligns with this condition. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
