state that parents believe lying is the most unforgivable moral problem. Therefore, this option cannot be confirmed as true based on the given information.\n\nC) Most parents are more than willing to solve the problem of children lying.\n- The context states that "many parents will encounter the problem of their children lying or concealing the truth," but it does not explicitly state that most parents are more than willing to solve the problem of children lying. Therefore, this option cannot be confirmed as true based on the given information.\n\nD) Children\'s behavior of concealing their own situation has not attracted the attention of parents.\n- The context states that "the problem of children concealing their own situation from their parents is not only worse solved, but also not given enough attention," which implies that children\'s behavior of concealing their own situation has not attracted the attention of parents. Therefore, this option can be confirmed as true based on the given information. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
