e setting high standards for employees and encouraging them to work with high quality demonstrate a desire to achieve excellence in leadership.\n\n4. **Option D**: Xiao Wang, a high school student, keeps reviewing the questions he had made wrong in the past, hoping he would not make any more mistakes in the college entrance exam.\n   - This option does not align with the definition because reviewing past mistakes and hoping not to make them again does not necessarily indicate a desire to achieve success or excellence in one's academic performance. It is more about avoiding failure rather than striving for achievement.\n\nBased on this analysis, the correct answer is:. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
