wledge to solve problems in exams. This is not typical intuitive thinking because it involves using knowledge to solve problems rather than making quick guesses or assumptions.\n\nD) The doctor quickly made a diagnosis of the disease based on the patient's oral materials.\n- This option describes a quick and intuitive approach to making a diagnosis. The doctor uses the patient's oral materials (such as symptoms and medical history) to make a quick and preliminary diagnosis. This is typical intuitive thinking because it involves making a quick and preliminary judgment based on limited information. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
