messages:   55%|#####5    | 330/600 [09:48<02:05,  2.14it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIn most cases, writing poems and filling words is a process of mutual accommodation between language and emotion. It is unpredictable for a beginner to have what kind of feelings and choose what kind of sentence pattern to start with. But once he has a preliminary idea, he can always get appropriate help in the book Tang and Song Poetry Rhythms. He will know which words are suitable to express what kind of feelings, what kind of rhyme he should choose, and how to make rational use of certain rhetorical devices so as not to be fooled in the face of special syntax. If you have read enough ancient poems and have a certain sense of language, you will indeed be able to complete your first creation with the help of this book. It can not teach people to write amazing masterpieces, but with the greatest sincerity to prevent you from making all kinds of jokes.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings is the main content of this text?\n# Options:\nA) Tang and song poetry rhythms is suitable for beginners because of its rich tones\nB) Poetry creation is essentially a process of mutual accommodation between language and emotion\nC) Tang and song poetry rhythms provides a very good help for beginners\nD) The creator of poetry must have abundant emotion and high literary accomplishment', '<think>.\nTo determine the main content of the text, let\'s break down the information provided step by step:.\n\n1. The text discusses the process of writing poems and filling words, which involves mutual accommodation between language and emotion.\n2. It mentions that beginners may struggle with choosing the right words and sentence patterns, but they can find help in the book "Tang and Song Poetry Rhythms.".\n3. The book helps beginners by providing guidance on suitable words, rhyme, and rhetorical devices to avoid making mistakes.\n4. The text emphasizes that while the book cannot teach people to write amazing masterpieces, it can prevent beginners from making all kinds of jokes.\n\nBased on these points, the main content of the text is that "Tang and Song Poetry Rhythms" provides a very good help for beginners in the process of writing poems and filling words. Therefore, the correct answer is:. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
