gument's conclusion about the number of planets fit to sustain life. The argument focuses on the number of planets in the universe, not the similarity of our solar system to others.\n\nD) Most other planetary systems in the universe have nine planets.\n- This option is not directly related to the argument's conclusion about the number of planets fit to sustain life. The argument focuses on the number of planets in the universe, not the number of planets in specific systems.\n\nBased on this analysis, the option that the argument presumes without providing justification is:. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
