: "The school board president has the authority to offer the faculty their desired salary increase." This assumption is not necessary because the context does not provide information about the school board president\'s authority.\n   - **Option C**: "The faculty of Grey County Public Schools will not be going on strike." This assumption is not necessary because the context explicitly states that the faculty will go on strike unless their salary is increased.\n   - **Option D**: "The faculty of Grey County Public Schools will not accept a package of improved benefits in place of their desired wage increase." This assumption is necessary because it directly relates to the faculty\'s willingness to accept a different form of compensation (improved benefits) instead of a wage increase. If the faculty does not accept this alternative, then the only remaining option is to cut after-school programs.\n\nBased on this analysis, the correct answer is **Option D**. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
