ood can have a parent with type B blood.\n   - **Option C:** "People with type B blood will always have children with type O blood.".\n     - This option is incorrect because the student\'s example shows that a child with type O blood can have a parent with type B blood.\n   - **Option D:** "If both parents have type B blood, their children will also have type B blood.".\n     - This option is correct because the student\'s example shows that a child with type O blood can have parents with type B blood, which contradicts the professor\'s statement that if both parents have type O blood, their children\'s blood type can only be type O.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct answer is:. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
