messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIf you close all the wrong doors, truth will be shut out.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is closest to the meaning of the above judgement?\n# Options:\nA) If truth is shut out, it must be that you close all the wrong doors.\nB) Truth can not be shut out unless all the doors of wrong are closed.\nC) If the truth is not shut out, then the door to all wrong must not be closed.\nD) To accept the truth, we must reject wrong.', '<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the given statement and analyze each option step by step:.\n\n**Given Statement:** "If you close all the wrong doors, truth will be shut out.".\n\nThis statement can be rephrased as:.\n- If (you close all the wrong doors), then (truth will be shut out).\n\nNow, let\'s examine each option:.\n\n**Option A:** "If truth is shut out, it must be that you close all the wrong doors.".\n- This option is the contrapositive of the given statement. The contrapositive of "If P, then Q" is "If not Q, then not P". In this case, the contrapositive would be "If truth is not shut out, then you did not close all the wrong doors". This is not the same as the given statement, so Option A is incorrect.\n\n**Option B:** "Truth can not be shut out unless all the doors of wrong are closed.".\n- This option is the converse of the given statement. The converse of "If P, then Q" is "If Q, then P". In this case, the converse would be "If truth is shut out, then you closed all the wrong doors". Therefore, my final option is: ']]
