rents on land.\n- This option highlights the difficulty in understanding ocean currents compared to land-based air currents. It supports the notion that scientists know less about the undersea environment due to the complexity of studying ocean currents.\n\nC) In contrast to most terrestrial environments, sea-level temperature conditions are generally stable and consistent because sunlight can not penetrate deep below sea level.\n- This option explains why sea-level temperature conditions are stable, but it does not directly address the difficulty in studying the undersea environment. It provides a reason for the stability but does not support the overall discussion about the lack of knowledge.\n\nD) Very few people have seen detailed maps of sea floor extensions, even though such maps can be seen in almost every major library.\n- This option suggests that despite the availability of detailed maps, they are not widely accessible or understood. This supports the idea that scientists know less about the undersea environment due to the limited accessibility of information. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
