.\n\nB) Professor Zhang has never bought a house. He believes that buying a house is not as good as renting a house, and renting a house is not as good as borrowing a house.\n- This statement reflects Professor Zhang's personal preference rather than his financial situation, so it does not fit the characteristics of the sandwich layer.\n\nC) Lao Liu used his life savings to buy a second-hand house with three bedrooms and one living room.\n- This option describes Lao Liu buying a house with his life savings, which does not align with the characteristics of the sandwich layer, as they are unable to buy houses outside of government guarantees and the market.\n\nD) Xiao Li, Xiao Wang, and Xiao Liu who have just been recruited by the company live in a temporary warehouse of the company. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
